<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rdf:RDF xmlns:cc="http://creativecommons.org/ns#" xmlns:dct="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:adms="http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#" xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/" xmlns:odrl="http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/" xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:dcat="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#" xmlns:lcon="http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#" xmlns:sioc="http://rdfs.org/sioc/ns#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#" xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xmlns:schema="http://schema.org/" xmlns:v="http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#" xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/" xmlns:voaf="http://purl.org/vocommons/voaf#" xmlns:wdrs="http://www.w3.org/2007/05/powder-s#" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#" xmlns:spdx="http://spdx.org/rdf/terms#" xmlns:time="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#" xmlns:dcatap="http://data.europa.eu/r5r/" xmlns:stat="http://data.europa.eu/s1n/statdcat-ap/" xmlns:qb="http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#" ><dcat:Dataset rdf:about="http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-datasets/-/sdg_12_31"><dct:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-06-11</dct:issued><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Fußabdruck des Verbrauchs</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Consumption footprint</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Empreinte de consommation</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Zeitliche Frequenz</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Time frequency</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Fréquence (relative au temps)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Geopolitische Meldeeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Geopolitical entity (reporting)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Entité géopolitique (déclarante)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Maßeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Unit of measure</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Unité de mesure</dcat:keyword><dct:type><skos:Concept  rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/dataset-type/STATISTICAL"/></dct:type><dct:title xml:lang="en">Consumption footprint - single weighted score</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="en">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;The consumption footprint is a set of 16 life cycle assessment (LCA)-based indicators to assess the environmental impacts of the EU and its Member States consumption by combining data on consumption intensity and environmental impacts of representative products. It is based on the combination of: (a) the emissions to air, soil and water as well as the resources used along the life cycle of around 165 representative products, belonging to 5 areas of consumption (food, mobility, housing, household goods, and appliances), (b) the consumption intensities of those products, which are calculated based on consumption statistics, and (c) the Environmental Footprint (EF) impact assessment method, which translates emissions and resource consumption into 16 potential environmental impacts that can be aggregated into a single score. The EF impact indicators can be compared with a set of thresholds that are based on the Planetary Boundaries framework. Thus the single weighted score measures the number of times that the planetary boundary is transgressed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Empreinte de consommation - note unique pondérée</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="fr">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;L’empreinte de la consommation est un ensemble de 16 indicateurs fondés sur l’évaluation du cycle de vie (ACV) visant à évaluer les incidences environnementales de la consommation de l’UE et de ses États membres en combinant les données sur l’intensité de la consommation et les incidences environnementales des produits représentatifs. Il est basé sur la combinaison de: (a) les émissions dans l’air, le sol et l’eau ainsi que les ressources utilisées tout au long du cycle de vie d’environ 165 produits représentatifs, appartenant à 5 secteurs de consommation (nourriture, mobilité, logement, biens ménagers et appareils), (b) les intensités de consommation de ces produits, qui sont calculées sur la base des statistiques de consommation, et (c) la méthode d’évaluation de l’impact de l’empreinte environnementale (EF), qui traduit les émissions et la consommation de ressources en 16 impacts potentiels sur l’environnement qui peuvent être agrégés en un seul score. Les indicateurs d’impact de l’EE peuvent être comparés à un ensemble de seuils basés sur le cadre des limites planétaires. Ainsi, le score unique pondéré mesure le nombre de fois où la frontière planétaire est transgressée.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="de">Fußabdruck des Konsum - Gesamtwirkungsindikator, gewichtet</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="de">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;Der Verbrauchsfußabdruck ist eine Reihe von 16 Ökobilanzindikatoren zur Bewertung der Umweltauswirkungen der EU und ihrer Mitgliedstaaten, indem Daten über die Verbrauchsintensität und die Umweltauswirkungen repräsentativer Produkte kombiniert werden. Es basiert auf der Kombination von: A) die Emissionen in Luft, Boden und Wasser sowie die Ressourcen, die während des Lebenszyklus von rund 165 repräsentativen Produkten verwendet werden, die zu fünf Verbrauchsbereichen (Lebensmittel, Mobilität, Wohnen, Haushaltswaren und Geräte) gehören, b) die Verbrauchsintensitäten dieser Produkte, die auf der Grundlage von Verbrauchsstatistiken berechnet werden, und c) die Folgenabschätzungsmethode für den Umweltfußabdruck (EF), die Emissionen und Ressourcenverbrauch in 16 potenzielle Umweltauswirkungen umsetzt, die in einem einzigen Score zusammengefasst werden können. Die EF-Wirkungsindikatoren können mit einer Reihe von Schwellenwerten verglichen werden, die auf dem Planetary Boundaries Framework basieren. So misst der einzelne gewichtete Score die Anzahl der Male, in denen die planetare Grenze überschritten wird.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</dct:description><dct:identifier>sdg_12_31</dct:identifier><foaf:page rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/sdg_12_31"/><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EUR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BEL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BGR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CZE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DNK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DEU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EST"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/IRL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GRC"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ESP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FRA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HRV"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ITA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CYP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LVA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LTU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LUX"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HUN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MLT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NLD"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/AUT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/POL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/PRT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ROU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FIN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SWE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ISL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NOR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CHE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GBR"/></dct:spatial><stat